    <node id="Perikanan">
      <data key="d0">Perikanan</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">All activities related to the management and utilization of fish resources and their environment, starting from pre-production, production, processing, to marketing within a fisheries business system.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3f250dcbafd593c2d06ce016eeea9d5f-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1793612044</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sumber Daya Ikan">
      <data key="d0">Sumber Daya Ikan</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">Sumber Daya Ikan refers to the natural fish stocks and resources, encompassing the potential of all types of fish. These available fish resources serve as a primary subject for systematic data collection and ongoing management.

The management of Sumber Daya Ikan involves biological fish resources that are conserved, rehabilitated, and managed under specified principles. These resources are utilized for breeding, development, and the preservation of ecosystems, with a core focus on ensuring sustainability and environmental protection. Furthermore, Sumber Daya Ikan includes fish resources located both within and outside of Indonesian fishery management areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3f250dcbafd593c2d06ce016eeea9d5f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1ffff1f2e3dfa130e836c0fbbe361e57-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c5f272acc0b47431bf705b7bdfc55b34-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-efe29281cb29cea02a55dc6d4a656fe4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9b360d50b06bd57b4cb7c6ddbce56066-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0ad9a52ae6cc54180ac316dd4a815479-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2a7f63233750f66081316ef941910c77-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5d7cd3764e250ee42c04a925c49a740a-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1793622681</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lingkungan Sumber Daya Ikan">
      <data key="d0">Lingkungan Sumber Daya Ikan</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The waters where fish resources live, including biota and surrounding natural factors.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3f250dcbafd593c2d06ce016eeea9d5f-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1793612044</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Ikan">
      <data key="d0">Ikan</data>
      <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
      <data key="d2">All types of organisms whose entire or partial life cycle is in a water environment.&lt;SEP&gt;The aquatic organism that is the object of handling and processing.`&lt;SEP&gt;A type of aquatic animal that constitutes a specific form of fishery crime evidence.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3f250dcbafd593c2d06ce016eeea9d5f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7caa573ce907926dfb1d5d112debc427-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e36b555749beade4c744d39b6a9f5f42-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1793618162</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Penangkapan Ikan">
      <data key="d0">Penangkapan Ikan</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Activities to obtain fish in non-cultured waters using any tool or method, including using vessels for loading, transporting, storing, cooling, handling, processing, and/or preserving fish.&lt;SEP&gt;Activities involving the capture of fish.&lt;SEP&gt;The activity of catching fish in regulated maritime zones.&lt;SEP&gt;The activity of catching fish, which is recorded in daily reports.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3f250dcbafd593c2d06ce016eeea9d5f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2727039291ac2002dd3e3bacae49f9a1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5b92e3da08870a168c229ea3603a9355-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-505edc34f4b2995f33a1cb0504f5ee50-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1793622322</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pembudidayaan Ikan">
      <data key="d0">Pembudidayaan Ikan</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Activities to maintain, grow, and/or breed fish and harvest the results in a controlled environment, including using vessels for loading, transporting, storing, cooling, handling, processing, and/or preserving fish.&lt;SEP&gt;The activity of farming or cultivating fish.&lt;SEP&gt;Activities involving fish cultivation.&lt;SEP&gt;The cultivation of fish, which can be conducted in rivers, lakes, or seas.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3f250dcbafd593c2d06ce016eeea9d5f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ca77871eaf5880d4a99669013079d4d5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2727039291ac2002dd3e3bacae49f9a1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0ad9a52ae6cc54180ac316dd4a815479-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1793620791</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Konservasi Sumber Daya Ikan">
      <data key="d0">Konservasi Sumber Daya Ikan</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Efforts for the protection, preservation, and utilization of fish resources, including ecosystems, species, and genetics to ensure existence, availability, and sustainability while maintaining and improving the quality, value, and diversity of fish resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Measures and actions taken to preserve and protect fish resources.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3f250dcbafd593c2d06ce016eeea9d5f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-cffaac94ef2c2024bbb1488d40d770a4-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1793616110</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Kapal Perikanan">
      <data key="d0">Kapal Perikanan</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Kapal Perikanan refers to maritime vessels, ships, boats, or other floating tools utilized for a diverse range of activities within the fisheries sector. These activities encompass fish capture, support operations for fish capture, fish cultivation, transportation of fish, and fish processing. Furthermore, Kapal Perikanan may be utilized for fisheries training, as well as for fisheries research and exploration purposes.

In the context of Indonesian maritime regulations, Kapal Perikanan can specifically denote a fishing vessel owned by Indonesian citizens that operates both within Indonesian waters and on the high seas. To operate legally, such a vessel must obtain a fitness certificate, which is a mandatory prerequisite for receiving a sailing permit. This sailing permit must be secured before the vessel can engage in catching or transporting fish from a fishing port.

Additionally, Kapal Perikanan serves as a functional location where fishery supervisors can perform their official duties. Because these vessels are used for fishing activities, they are subject to regulatory oversight and may be inspected, stopped, or seized by a supervisor to ensure compliance with applicable laws and standards.&lt;SEP&gt;A fishing vessel that can be seized and handed over to cooperatives or collective business groups.&lt;SEP&gt;A vessel used for fishing activities.&lt;SEP&gt;The fishing vessels used in the industry.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3f250dcbafd593c2d06ce016eeea9d5f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-85d2e87907b665692f0b9b9f5dfd1285-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0838a3f46d9a0838a242a520f5182f23-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f3e28f0d7f60cc7a75874be8028f3f27-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9ff7709481fc713a6e71c843157c22d0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-234faf2c9eddf47d34fafb6f84b1b01d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-46a76389201b0a6d50af5e5091a79e2d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6163486fd141fd23207a47ad464aac20-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8b803ece93e21676851b0849b23c7ef4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-960d94c55d2317a253dca8fdbafce903-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5d7cd3764e250ee42c04a925c49a740a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7aded5d5e52a1e434667c92c52046b41-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1793623278</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nelayan">
      <data key="d0">Nelayan</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A person whose livelihood is performing fish capture.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals who are involved in fishing activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals who engage in fishing activities.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3f250dcbafd593c2d06ce016eeea9d5f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35609e3dadbb447e7323b8e7b23e171f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5d7cd3764e250ee42c04a925c49a740a-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1793622609</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nelayan Kecil">
      <data key="d0">Nelayan Kecil</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Nelayan Kecil refers to individuals whose primary livelihood is the capture of fish to meet their daily living needs. They are specifically defined as small-scale fishermen who operate fishing vessels with a maximum capacity of 5 gross tons.

Within the framework of fishery legislation, Nelayan Kecil are granted several regulatory benefits and exemptions. These include exemptions from specific license requirements, certain vessel monitoring requirements, and the fishery levy. Furthermore, they qualify for various other regulatory exemptions as stipulated by law.

While they are granted these exemptions, Nelayan Kecil are still subject to the rule of law and may face legal penalties for violating specific articles of the legislation. Despite these potential penalties, they are intentionally protected and prioritized by fishery legislation. Additionally, a key objective in fishery resource management is to improve the welfare and living standards of Nelayan Kecil through the implementation of optimal management practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Small-scale fishermen who are prioritized in equitable fishery management.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3f250dcbafd593c2d06ce016eeea9d5f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1ffff1f2e3dfa130e836c0fbbe361e57-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-75e0a9225f4cfb6419813f0b2ea4b76d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-78ed963f3dd3c00083f50735157dfe57-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-efe29281cb29cea02a55dc6d4a656fe4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4251617c6b8fa7a32e39c14c27e95a1a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1359332418ece67d5d88eef8516bfae6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7c49841464685c342625bf812725d84b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7c49841464685c342625bf812725d84b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9b360d50b06bd57b4cb7c6ddbce56066-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1793620707</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pembudi Daya Ikan">
      <data key="d0">Pembudi Daya Ikan</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">A person whose livelihood is performing fish cultivation.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals involved in fish aquaculture and farming.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3f250dcbafd593c2d06ce016eeea9d5f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5d7cd3764e250ee42c04a925c49a740a-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1793622609</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pembudi Daya-Ikan Kecil">
      <data key="d0">Pembudi Daya-Ikan Kecil</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Pembudi Daya-Ikan Kecil refers to small-scale fish farmers, breeders, or aquaculture farmers whose primary livelihood involves fish cultivation to meet their daily living needs. Within the framework of fishery legislation, these individuals are recognized as a priority group.

Due to the small-scale nature of their operations, Pembudi Daya-Ikan Kecil are granted various regulatory exemptions, including exemptions from certain vessel monitoring requirements and the fishery levy. Despite these specific exemptions, they remain subject to legal penalties for violating various articles of the law.

Furthermore, the welfare and living standards of Pembudi Daya-Ikan Kecil are intended to be improved through the implementation of optimal fishery resource management strategies.&lt;SEP&gt;Small-scale fish farmers who are prioritized in equitable fishery management.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3f250dcbafd593c2d06ce016eeea9d5f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1ffff1f2e3dfa130e836c0fbbe361e57-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-78ed963f3dd3c00083f50735157dfe57-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-efe29281cb29cea02a55dc6d4a656fe4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4251617c6b8fa7a32e39c14c27e95a1a-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1359332418ece67d5d88eef8516bfae6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7c49841464685c342625bf812725d84b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7c49841464685c342625bf812725d84b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9b360d50b06bd57b4cb7c6ddbce56066-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1793620707</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Setiap Orang">
      <data key="d0">Setiap Orang</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">An individual or a corporation.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals who are legally obligated to preserve and prohibited from damaging fish germplasm.&lt;SEP&gt;Any individual who is obligated to keep and store SIKPI Asli on a fish transport vessel.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-3f250dcbafd593c2d06ce016eeea9d5f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c5f272acc0b47431bf705b7bdfc55b34-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-130a45a160a3017c0ca1c8575057bcbd-chunk-000</data>
