    <node id="Pengawas Perikanan">
      <data key="d0">Pengawas Perikanan</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Pengawas Perikanan refers to civil servants who work specifically in the fisheries field and are appointed by the minister or a designated official. They serve as the body or individuals responsible for overseeing fishery activities, monitoring activities, and supervising the implementation of legal regulations across various fishery-related jurisdictions.

These officials are primarily tasked with the monitoring and enforcement of fishery regulations to ensure compliance within the sector. Their authority includes the power to inspect businesses, verify necessary documents, and enforce laws against fisheries crimes. Furthermore, Pengawas Perikanan are responsible for key administrative functions, such as issuing permits and providing fitness certificates for fishing vessels.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-f3e28f0d7f60cc7a75874be8028f3f27-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9ff7709481fc713a6e71c843157c22d0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2727039291ac2002dd3e3bacae49f9a1-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a2584d4d1ad82841bc89b193a8bd0dd5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-234faf2c9eddf47d34fafb6f84b1b01d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-46a76389201b0a6d50af5e5091a79e2d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6163486fd141fd23207a47ad464aac20-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7aded5d5e52a1e434667c92c52046b41-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1793623421</data>
